                        "glosses": [
                            "diminutive of недалеко́ (nedalekó): not far, not far away, not far off, nearby, close"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "diminutive",
                            "form-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "17a0b6eb-0c86-409f-a9d8-13acf4696566",
                                "sense_id": "26d12296-1e4b-396a-8126-e2be809cae95",
                                "text": "— Сказа́л бы слове́чко, да волк недале́чко, — сказа́л, нахму́рясь, Гаври́ла Афана́сьевич.",
                                "translation": "\"I'd add a word or two of my own, but even the walls have ears [literally, “the wolf is not far away”],\" said Gavrila Afanasevich, frowning.",
                                "english": "\"I'd add a word or two of my own, but even the walls have ears [literally, “the wolf is not far away”],\" said Gavrila Afanasevich, frowning."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30cf086c-63bc-4d4d-adf0-fcfc974273e7",
                                "sense_id": "26d12296-1e4b-396a-8126-e2be809cae95",
                                "text": "1848, Dmitrij Davydov, “Думы беглеца на Байкале (Thoughts of a Runaway in Baikal)”\nСла́вное мо́ре — приво́льный Байка́л,\nСла́вный кора́бль — омулёвая бо́чка.\nНу, Баргузи́н, пошеве́ливай вал,\nПлыть молодцу́ недале́чко!\nSlávnoje móre — privólʹnyj Bajkál,\nSlávnyj koráblʹ — omuljóvaja bóčka.\nNu, Barguzín, poševélivaj val,\nPlytʹ molodcú nedaléčko!\nGlorious sea – vast Baikal,\n[My] glorious boat – an omul barrel.\nWell, Barguzin, stir the billowing waves,\n[It's] not far off for a lad to float."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
